{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Add a Paywall","roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide takes you from a wired Swidux app to a fully gated feature with paywall presentation, entitlement observation, restore, and manage-subscription support. It covers state and action wiring, implementing a "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", presenting the sheet, gating a feature, and previewing in pro state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an API-level reference of every type and action, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Before-you-start","text":"Before you start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You have a Swidux app already wired up — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You have a purchase backend in mind. RevenueCat is the path of least resistance, but vanilla StoreKit or a custom server work just as well — the plugin doesn’t care.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPaywall\",","    ]",")"]},{"level":2,"text":"Step 2: Add state and actions","anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a paywall slice to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":", and a paywall case to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var paywall: PaywallState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ AppAction.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case paywall(PaywallAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"import SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is needed in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file that touches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.*"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"PaywallAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — including views that read the slice for display. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@_exported import Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns reducing for ","type":"text"},{"code":".paywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actions, so the root reducer should fall through:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .paywall:","    return nil"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-3-Provide-a-PaywallService","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Provide a `PaywallService`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin needs a "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that talks to your purchase backend. Pick the path that matches your backend.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Path A: RevenueCat (recommended)","type":"heading","anchor":"Path-A-RevenueCat-recommended"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},{"text":" companion package and use the supplied ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":". No bridging code on your side.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","","let service = RevenueCatPaywallService()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The companion package also ships "},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin. See its "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for configuration (API key, entitlement identifiers)."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Path B: StoreKit or custom backend","type":"heading","anchor":"Path-B-StoreKit-or-custom-backend"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For any non-RevenueCat backend, implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" directly. The protocol is small:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","struct MyPaywallService: PaywallService {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Fetch the current entitlement once.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot> {","        AsyncStream { continuation in","            \/\/ Yield a new snapshot each time the entitlement changes.","            \/\/ Call continuation.finish() when the source ends.","        }","    }","","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Run a restore against the user's account and return the result.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements"},{"type":"text","text":" and listens to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.updates"},{"type":"text","text":"; a custom server conformer hits whatever endpoint reports the user’s entitlement."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Previews and tests","type":"heading","anchor":"Previews-and-tests"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" for backend-agnostic previews:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let service = MockPaywallService(isPro: true)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’re on Path A, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" also ships "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" for RevenueCat-flavored previews."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Step 4: Wire the plugin","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-4-Wire-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Construct and register "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" inside your "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" factory:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","let paywallPlugin = PaywallPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.paywall,","    action: AppAction.paywall,","    extractAction: { if case .paywall(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    service: RevenueCatPaywallService()",")","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In production, wrap the service in "},{"code":"ResilientPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"transient entitlement-read failure at cold launch never gates a paid user as"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"free. Back its cache with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" (not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UserDefaults"},{"text":", whose","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plist a user can edit to spoof entitlements):"}]},{"code":["service: ResilientPaywallService(","    base: RevenueCatPaywallService(),","    store: KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.myapp\")",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reference (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"staleness policy and threat model.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-5-Observe-customer-info-on-launch","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Observe customer info on launch"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Start the long-lived entitlement stream once, on the root view:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .task { store.send(.paywall(.observeCustomerInfo)) }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"observeCustomerInfo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns an effect that lives for the duration of ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every snapshot the service yields flows through ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and updates ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.isPro","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasPermanentLicense","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-6-Present-the-paywall","level":2,"text":"Step 6: Present the paywall"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bind a sheet to ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.isPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and dispatch ","type":"text"},{"code":".paywall(.dismiss)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when it closes:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".sheet(isPresented: Binding(","    get: { store.paywall.isPresented },","    set: { if !$0 { store.send(.paywall(.dismiss)) } }",")) {","    PaywallSheet()","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Trigger presentation by dispatching ","type":"text"},{"code":".paywall(.request(reason:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a short identifier describing why you’re asking. The reason is stored in ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.requestedReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so the sheet can tailor its copy.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-7-Gate-a-feature","level":2,"text":"Step 7: Gate a feature"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallState.isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before running gated work. If it’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", dispatch ","type":"text"},{"code":".request","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Export PDF\") {","    if store.paywall.isGateSatisfied {","        store.send(.export(.exportPDF))","    } else {","        store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-8-Restore-purchases","level":2,"text":"Step 8: Restore purchases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a restore button to your paywall sheet. Reflect ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.isLoading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to disable it while the call is in flight:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Restore Purchases\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.restorePurchases))","}",".disabled(store.paywall.isLoading)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On success, the resulting snapshot flows through ","type":"text"},{"code":".customerInfoUpdated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and updates the gate. On failure, ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.paywall.error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is set.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-9-Manage-subscriptions","level":2,"text":"Step 9: Manage subscriptions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an existing subscriber, surface a button that deep-links into the system subscription management page:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["Button(\"Manage Subscription\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.openManageSubscriptions))","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This opens ","type":"text"},{"code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" via the plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"openURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handler, which routes to the App Store on iOS and Settings on macOS.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Testing","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"MockPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to drive previews and tests into a known entitlement state:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["#Preview(\"Pro\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService(isPro: true)","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}","","#Preview(\"Free\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService()","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Plumb the service through a parameter on your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory so previews can override it without touching the live RevenueCat SDK.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","title":"Add a Parental Gate","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"link"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","abstract":[{"text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","abstract":[{"text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","title":"Add iCloud Sync","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToCancelEffects":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects","abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","title":"Cancel Effects","role":"article"},"https://heirloomlogic.github.io/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall/documentation/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall/":{"identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DocC reference"}],"url":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","title":"DocC reference","type":"link"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"abstract":[{"text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Security Posture","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","title":"Add Feature Flags","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"abstract":[{"text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro — no hand-written ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" classes, database actors, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","role":"article","title":"Add Persistence","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","title":"Add Analytics","type":"topic","kind":"article"}}}